RULING ON RECORD (internal use only): the redislib modules are compiled into
skynetjit as an in-process data-structure library used by our own services. They
are not offered to third parties as a service, and skynetjit builds containing
them are not distributed outside the company. Under that reading RSALv2 permits
the use, which is why this port takes the RSALv2 branch of the tri-license and
does not trigger SSPLv1/AGPLv3 network-copyleft obligations. If redislib ever
becomes part of something shipped to, or hosted for, third parties, this ruling
must be revisited before that happens -- the safest fallback is AGPLv3.

